## 9. Component standards

For each component, define:

- **Anatomy** — parts.
- **States** — default, hover, focus-visible, active, disabled, loading, error.
- **Sizes** — sm / md / lg.
- **Variants** — primary / secondary / ghost / destructive.
- **Don'ts** — anti-patterns.

Required components:

- Button (`<<BUTTON_NOTES>>`)
- Input + label (`<<INPUT_NOTES>>`)
- Select (`<<SELECT_NOTES>>`)
- Modal / dialog (`<<MODAL_NOTES>>`)
- Toast / snackbar (`<<TOAST_NOTES>>`)
- Card (`<<CARD_NOTES>>`)
- Table (`<<TABLE_NOTES>>`)
- Badge / status pill (`<<BADGE_NOTES>>`)
- Avatar (`<<AVATAR_NOTES>>`)
- Empty state (`<<EMPTY_STATE_NOTES>>`)

## 10. Page-level rules

- Every page has: header, primary content area, optional sidebar, optional footer.
- Every page handles loading, empty, error explicitly (see `CODING_RULES.md` §4).
- Every page has a clear primary action.

## 11. Accessibility

- WCAG target: **<<WCAG_LEVEL>>**.
- All interactive elements keyboard reachable.
- Focus ring visible on `:focus-visible`.
- Colour is never the only signal — pair with text or icon.
- Form errors announced via `aria-describedby`.

